  },
  question: "CLOSED for the model half: srv11_host_lan_endpoint is deleted, on the operator's Group B sale ruling of 2026-10-10 (gunbc.spark.dgx_procurement::dgx_spark_group_b_sale_2026_10_10), so the ledger no longer answers that a sold cage holds 192.168.1.238. What stays with another change, and is NOT claimed closed here: 192.168.1.238 becomes srv14/butch's dated lease observation in the tailnet-anchor work (PR #16655), and srv11's HostIdentity row stays in gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_identity on purpose -- a sold unit may remain in the register as history, which is the difference between an identity and an endpoint. The retirement was done by deleting the declaration, not by leaving it outside the roster: three of those rows sitting unrostered is exactly how two holders on one address stayed invisible to every executed check (see three_spark_lan_endpoint_rows_answer_their_addresses_twice).",
